  "note": "A valley between ridge lines, the road along it: a narrow valley is held on the side spurs and hill features both sides in successive posns; a broad one also on the valley bed, strong at the mouth (MW s12 para 16 pp 161-162). A and B Coys on the side spurs; C Coy a second line on the left; 12 Pl on the valley bed; D Coy less 12 Pl the reserve. Strong points with all round defence, at least a Pl strong point in each Coy posn on its most dominating feature with 30 days' staying power; tiers from the foothills or valleys to the ridge, the final battle on the ridge (MW s12 paras 8-9 p 152). Frontage on IBB's extended row (MW prints no figure).",
